-- | A value's rendering as source that reads back: `spell(v)` is Curios text that denotes `v` at its type — a literal, or a constructor spelled by its type's own name, `Ordering/lt()` — which re-parses wherever the type's name is visible unqualified, the one place a value of it can be written at all, and reads in a test report as the author would have written it. `Show` stays the human-facing display; the two coincide only where a value's display already is its literal.
pub mod Spell;
pub use Spell/{let Spell};

